FreeBSD on the Pro1X: telepathy-ring for SMS only (built with
-DRING_SMS_ONLY, freebsd/hildon/apps.sh). The calls stay with sphone,
which talks to oFono's VoiceCallManager (pro1x-modemd) itself, as before.
FreeBSD's Hildon has no Telepathy call UI (Leste's voicecall-qt5 is not
built), so nothing would handle ring's call channels, and Mission Control
closes a channel no client handles, which for an incoming call of ring is
a hangup (and for one sphone dials, too). Without the call service's type
ring ignores the modem's VoiceCallManager ("ignoring interface"): no call
channels, no call agent; the media and conference managers are as without
a modem (no call channel classes).

--- a/src/ring-connection-manager.c
+++ b/src/ring-connection-manager.c
@@ -105,5 +105,13 @@
 
   modem_oface_register_type (MODEM_TYPE_SIM_SERVICE);
   modem_oface_register_type (MODEM_TYPE_SMS_SERVICE);
+  /* FreeBSD on the Pro1X: SMS only. Calls stay with sphone, which talks to
+   * oFono's VoiceCallManager itself; there is no Telepathy call UI to
+   * handle ring's call channels, and Mission Control closes a channel no
+   * client handles, which for ring's call channels is a hangup. So the
+   * VoiceCallManager is not an interface ring takes ("ignoring interface"):
+   * no call channels, no call agent. */
+#ifndef RING_SMS_ONLY
   modem_oface_register_type (MODEM_TYPE_CALL_SERVICE);
+#endif
 }
